#### Step 6: Configure Sampling Strategies

**Probability-Based Sampling (10%)**:
```csharp
// Sample 10% of all traces randomly
builder.Services.AddOpenTelemetry()
    .WithTracing(tracing => tracing
        .SetSampler(new TraceIdRatioBasedSampler(0.1))
    );
```

**Parent-Based Sampling (respect upstream decision)**:
```csharp
// If parent span sampled, sample child; otherwise apply probability
builder.Services.AddOpenTelemetry()
    .WithTracing(tracing => tracing
        .SetSampler(new ParentBasedSampler(new TraceIdRatioBasedSampler(0.1)))
    );
```

**Always-On Sampling (100% for critical services)**:
```csharp
// Sample all traces (use for low-volume critical services)
builder.Services.AddOpenTelemetry()
    .WithTracing(tracing => tracing
        .SetSampler(new AlwaysOnSampler())
    );
```

**Custom Sampling by Route**:
```csharp
public class CustomSampler : Sampler
{
    public override SamplingResult ShouldSample(in SamplingParameters samplingParameters)
    {
        // Always sample payment transactions
        if (samplingParameters.Tags.Any(t => t.Key == "http.route" && t.Value?.ToString()?.Contains("/api/payments") == true))
        {
            return new SamplingResult(SamplingDecision.RecordAndSample);
        }

        // Always sample error traces
        if (samplingParameters.Tags.Any(t => t.Key == "http.status_code" && Convert.ToInt32(t.Value) >= 500))
        {
            return new SamplingResult(SamplingDecision.RecordAndSample);
        }

        // Sample 10% of other traces
        return new TraceIdRatioBasedSampler(0.1).ShouldSample(samplingParameters);
    }
}

builder.Services.AddOpenTelemetry()
    .WithTracing(tracing => tracing
        .SetSampler(new CustomSampler())
    );
```

